Fork and modification notice

Syngle Observatory is a hard fork of RustGIS (https://github.com/opengeos/RustGIS), Copyright the
RustGIS contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The fork is owned by Syngle,
is changed freely and is never merged back; upstream is read-only.

Files in this repository have been modified for the fork: the product name ("Syngle Observatory"),
the application id (com.syngle.observatory), every user-visible string and the interface
translations, the web page and its manifest, the packaging metadata for every platform, and the
community, website, plugin-registry and download addresses of the upstream project (the fork has no
website, community forum, plugin registry, asset host or download mirror of its own, so commands
that need one require an explicit address). Two hosts upstream also uses are still read, because
the fork has no mirror for them: the build fetches the Natural Earth sample data from the upstream
asset host (`assets.rustgis.app/data`, set `RUSTGIS_DATA_DIR` to build offline), and the GeoLibre tool
releases and planet basemaps come from the opengeos project (`opengeos/geolibre-rust` releases and
`tiles.geolibre.app`), which are third-party works, not fork infrastructure. The upstream project's
icon, logo and brand assets were not carried over. The two licence-relevant files, LICENSE
(Apache-2.0, unchanged) and ATTRIBUTION.md (every third-party work, unmodified), are kept, and the
upstream project is credited there and in both About views (desktop and browser).

Changes specific to the fork, beyond the rename: `rustgis-web` gains a `canvas-only` feature (the
map view alone, no egui chrome; ADR 0010), and `crates/observatory-engine` is the native engine
sidecar moved out of `syngle-spike/engine` (#43) into a fork crate with tests. See the fork's
ticket and the Syngle-Ecosystem repository for the decisions.
